Package: behavSSF
Title: Guided Behavioural State Assessment for Step Selection Models
Version: 0.1.0.9004
Date: 2026-11-06
Authors@R: c(
    person("Aurélien", "Nicosia", email = "aurelien.nicosia@mat.ulaval.ca",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = "Adapted the research functions for the package and added visualisations, result summaries and configurable state taxonomies"),
    person("Ilhem", "Bouderbala", role = "aut", comment = "Original research functions and published methodological framework"),
    person("Daniel", "Fortin", role = "ctb", comment = "Published methodological framework"))
Description: A development implementation of hidden Markov step selection
    likelihoods, segmented state decoding, multistart fitting, and explicit
    ecological assessment rules. Implements a reference workflow based on
    Bouderbala, Nicosia and Fortin (2026) <doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0360547>.
    Kernel conventions are explicit and failed candidate models remain visible.
    Supports homogeneous transitions and, for exact two-state models on
    hourly data, daily cycles in transitions and mean step length, as well as
    state-specific lag effects. Compatible gamma-von Mises kernels are
    normalised analytically and can include a prospective target effect.
    An analytic-gradient engine and an R reference implementation are provided.
URL: https://aureliennicosiaulaval.github.io/behavSSF/, https://github.com/AurelienNicosiaULaval/behavSSF
